                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">71b4930f-9d10-41fd-ac4a-6b289cb862fc</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">About this file</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Kinetic units on a surface you draw. The set-up here is the Al Bahar Towers unit (Aedas, Abu Dhabi 2012): a honeycomb of
hexagonal cells sharing their frame bars, six petals per cell hinged on the frame, one linear actuator per unit at the
centre driving a hub through struts, deployed by how squarely the sun strikes each cell's own normal (Sun: one vector
per step). Every part meets the next without penetrating it (checked 1 Nov). Shape iris or louvre for the other
mechanisms; Csv is the actuator table. Replace Geo with your surface.
Pattern Studio, ARCH 540, Balreet Dhatt, 1 November 2026.</item>
                  </items>
